      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. We've also seen some cases with very strange, almost \"crusty\" or pebbled textures on the surface that look almost like they are protruding in irregular, small clusters. When the morphology gets that granular or uneven, are there specific descriptors in the ICD-10-CM dermatological section that better capture those physical irregularities, or do we just default to a more general \"skin disorder\" code if the texture is too non-standard?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
