      "content": "Okay, that makes sense. One thing that's throwing the team off is when the lesions appear in these small, almost aggressive-looking patches that seem to \"encroach\" on healthy tissue in a way that's hard to map to typical inflammatory models. Could you give me a few examples of specific ICD-10 categories or terms that deal with these types of aggressive, irregular, or \"encroaching\" morphological patterns? Just to make sure we're hitting the right level of clinical specificity.",
